---
import Product from '../../layouts/Product.astro';
import RenderLicenceIllustration from '../../components/RenderLicenceIllustration.astro';
import { products } from '../../data/products';
const product = products.find((p) => p.key === 'render')!;
---
<Product
  product={product}
  heading="Generate and sign your service’s documents."
  description="Create PDF licences, certificates, letters and receipts from your service’s data and approved templates. Add a digital seal with your institution’s signing key, with a timestamp when configured."
  note="Open-source document generation and signing. For a new service or one you already run."
>
  <section id="product-example" class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="render-example-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">One example: a professional licence</p>
        <h2 id="render-example-title">Create the licence document and apply your institution’s seal.</h2>
        <p>After your authority grants a licence, your service sends the holder’s details and licence terms to Registry Render. It generates and signs the document; your service stores it and makes it available to the holder.</p>
      </div>
      <RenderLicenceIllustration />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="render-capabilities-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Practical capabilities</p>
        <h2 id="render-capabilities-title">Prepare a consistent document, then sign it.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="product-facts">
        <article><h3>Use approved templates</h3><p>Define the layout, labels, fonts and supported languages. Package the reviewed template so the service uses a known version.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Check the required information</h3><p>Set the data each document needs. Render checks the supplied information against that definition before generating the PDF.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Sign with your institution’s key</h3><p>Apply a digital seal to the generated PDF. Recipients can validate the signature against your institution’s certificate and check for changes to the signed content. Add a timestamp from your configured authority.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="fit" class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="render-fit-title">
    <div class="section-inner product-fit">
      <div class="section-heading compact">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it fits your service</p>
        <h2 id="render-fit-title">Add document generation and signing beside your records.</h2>
        <p>Your application can request a generated and signed document from Render’s service. For generation alone, use a local command or embed Render in software. Data may come from <a href="/products/base-registry/">Base Registry Engine</a> or another system.</p>
      </div>
      <dl>
        <dt>Your institution defines the document and seal</dt><dd>Agree the content, template and when the service may issue it. For signing, configure the certificate, authorized applications and a key held in Vault or OpenBao Transit. Timestamping uses your chosen authority.</dd>
        <dt>The application keeps and shares the result</dt><dd>Your implementation stores the PDF and its identifying hashes, then provides the download, printing or document-access route people need.</dd>
        <dt>Choose who runs it</dt><dd>Your institution or appointed provider can host and operate Render, or we can run it for you. We quote hosting and operation separately in the proposal.</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="developers" class="section" aria-labelledby="render-developers-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading compact">
        <p class="eyebrow">Evaluate the software</p>
        <h2 id="render-developers-title">Generate your first document.</h2>
        <p>The tutorial generates a local letter and then requests a PDF through the service interface. The <a href="https://docs.registrystack.org/start/registry-render/">Render overview</a> explains the product; the <a href="https://docs.registrystack.org/operate/registry-render/">operations guide</a> covers running it. Follow <a href="https://docs.registrystack.org/operate/registry-render/#seal-documents">the signing setup</a> to apply a PAdES digital seal, with or without a timestamp. The guide includes a test seal to evaluate locally and the requirements for your institution’s signing key.</p>
        <p><a class="inline-cta" href={product.tutorialHref}>{product.tutorialLabel} →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Product>
